body:
Before I send the diff, one conflict you should decide on.

vcu/test_v40/t_v40.c:1642-1656 ("three commands skipped") sends a GCE CMD_WRITE to 0x16001000 and expects gce_skipped + 3, comment "inside VCU but no RWVC window". The DEC04 deliverable makes 0x16000000+0x30000 a window (RWVC_WIN_VDEC_ALL), and DEC02s page list has 0x16001000 as a real VDEC page (VDEC_PROTOCOL.md section 4). Any correct rev-3 mapping makes that address valid, so that one check fails by design: 0x16001000 now lands in VDEC_ALL (offset 0x1000), 0x17040000 and 0x40000000 are still skipped (+2).

There is no honest way to keep the unmodified suite green: either the window does not cover the gap (defeats the package) or the expectation changes. My patch file will therefore carry two hunks against your files: the production change (n2vcu.c, n2vcu.h) and this test expectation. Exact proposed test change (t_v40.c only):

  -	cmd_set(c, 0, CMD_WRITE, 0x16001000u, 1, 0xffffffffu);   /* inside VCU but no RWVC window */
  +	cmd_set(c, 0, CMD_WRITE, 0x16001000u, 1, 0xffffffffu);   /* DEC04: VDEC_ALL page 0x1000 */
   	cmd_set(c, 1, CMD_WRITE, 0x17040000u, 1, 0xffffffffu);   /* outside every VCU window */
   	cmd_set(c, 2, CMD_WRITE, 0x40000000u, 1, 0xffffffffu);   /* >= MAP_PA_BASE_1GB */
   	cmd_count(c, 3);
  ...
  -	ck_u64("no ops for skipped commands", e->f.nops, nops);
  +	ck_u64("one op for the DEC04 page", e->f.nops, nops + 1);
  ...
  -	ck_u64("three commands skipped", stats_of(e).gce_skipped, s.gce_skipped + 3);
  +	ck_u64("two commands skipped", stats_of(e).gce_skipped, s.gce_skipped + 2);
  +	ck_u64("0x16001000 reached VDEC_ALL", e->f.ops[nops].win, RWVC_WIN_VDEC_ALL);

Tell me if you prefer a different adaptation (e.g. use 0x1600c000, which is still outside every page) and I will use exactly that. My acceptance run applies dec04.patch + this test hunk to a /tmp mirror and runs your unmodified run_tests.sh; I will report both the patched-suite result and the one expected failure without the test hunk.

Second question, for your call: vcu_reg_lookup() serves both guest MMIO and GCE command addresses. I plan one entry, both paths, because DEC02s trace may show GCE writes into the gaps (DEC facts section 3 says MMIO vs GCE for the decoder is still [I]). Say if you want VDEC_ALL only in the MMIO path instead; I see no reason and it would hide a real access.

Write-combining: default OFF as you asked, setter n2vcu_set_write_combining(v,on), stats appended (hw_regs_calls + wc_* counters), flush before guest read, GCE ioctl entry, power, wait_irq, poll, sub-word/unaligned access, close/destroy, or at 256 ops. Full diff follows within the hour; header rev 3 is not in the tree yet, so the patch uses the real constant and my /tmp staging adds the proposed enum line only.
